ELECTRON RECOMBINATION OF HYDROGEN
hrecombine.nc

Data are taken directly from two DEGAS-format files: ehr1.dat and ehr2.dat.
Both were generated by versions of the Weisheit code, irls. Revisions
made to the code by Daren Stotler have been recorded in the CVS archive
"collrad". 

  --Version 2.0--
The file ehr1.dat corresponds to the file fort.18 in the repository,
revision 1.1. The generating code (and the data file) have the tag
r1_5. Relative to the original Weisheit code, this version has changes
made by Detlev Reiter to remove the steady-state assumption of recombination
equalling ionization. It also has Stotler's improvements to the "coupling
to continuum" contributions and energy exchange in recombination. This
file has also been widely used with the old DEGAS code. 

  --Version 2.1--
The file ehr2.dat is the latest version of the file, revision 1.12,
tag r1_13. The difference relative to ehr1.dat is the usage of the
Janev-Smith cross sections in the Weisheit code.

Both files have been altered slightly relative to the code-generated
versions, mainly by replacing ionization rates < 1.e-100 with 1.e-99.

   --Version 2.2--
Never did actually generate V. 2.1. This and subsequent versions should
come from ehr2.dat. The primary change here is the use of specific variables
for the energy and H-alpha rates following a standard scheme set up
for scoring. In particular, these data have implicit in them the 
ionization energy, 3->2 transition energy and Einstein coefficient,
as well as the H-alpha wavelengths. For more details, see reactionwrite.web.
(Should be V. 1.12). Current hionize.nc and hrecombine.nc files.

   --Version 2.3--
Same as V. 2.2, but with the OLDER ehr1.dat file. Generated this version
solely for backward compatibility and comparisons. Note that the netCDF file
has a different name. Named hionize1.nc and hrecombine1.nc for now; kept
around for backward compatibility.

   --Version 2.4--
Modified reactionwrite (v. 1.15) to fill unused data values with real_unused.

