MOLECULAR HYDROGEN DISSOCIATIVE IONIZATION
h2dision.nc

  --Version 2.0--
The file itself was generated by ratecalc, revision 1.26, using h2dision.input,
revision 1.1 as the input file. The reaction rate data are taken
from the Janev book and the associated Aladdin data. Because of 
restrictions on the fit, the first six and last four values come out
0. Paste in their values from the DEGAS file, atmc.dat. The dissociation
energy and electron energy loss values represent a linear fit to the
temperature dependent prescription given in the Janev book. 
Note that the latter is correct regardless of the energy of the
second electron since said energy remains within the electron fluid.

  --Version 2.1--
This file was generated as above using h2dision.input (should be version 1.2).
Modifications made to the rate as above. Manually edited units, multiplier,
and added "table_external" data. The dissociation energy is as above.
To be consistent with the other data files, we needed to put the background
energy loss rate on the same grid as the reaction rate. In so doing,
the original Janev prescription becomes very simple: loss rate is
18.5 eV per reaction below electron temperatures of 17 eV. Is 33.6 eV
for T_e > 31 eV, and scales as 1.5 T_e for the two temperature values in
between these limits.

