MOLECULAR HYDROGEN ION DISSOCIATIVE RECOMBINATION
h2pdisrec.nc

  --Version 2.0--
The file itself was generated by ratecalc, revision 1.26, using h2disrec.input,
revision 1.1 as the input file. The reaction rate data are taken
from the Janev book and the associated Aladdin data. Because of 
restrictions on the fit, the last four values come out
0. Paste in their values from the DEGAS file, atmc.dat. The dissociation
energy and electron energy loss values DIFFER from the Janev book. The former
comes from a private communication by Janev stating that the dissociation
energy should be 0.5*(8.6 + 13.6/n**2); with n = 3 (the dominant pathway),
this is 5.1 eV. The electron energy loss is given by 1.5 T_{e} / 1.7; the
1.7 comes from averaging the electron energy over the cross section 
(shown by Reiter, 1992 PSI).

  --Version 2.1--
As part of the scoring implementation, switch from an energy loss term
to an energy loss rate (multiply energy loss as above by rate). Add 
explicit H-alpha emission rate and separate wavelengths for each
isotope (as elsewhere). The expression used for the former is: \[
f_{n=3} \frac{A_{3 \rightarrow 2}}{( A_{3 \rightarrow 2} + A_{3 \rightarrow 2}
)} E_{3 \rightarrow 2} S_{dis},
\]
where: $f_{n=3} = 0.45$ (Janev book), 
$A_{3 \rightarrow 2} = 4.410 \times 10^{7}$ s$^{-1}$,
$A_{3 \rightarrow 1} = 5.575 \times 10^{7}$ s$^{-1}$
(this ratio was previously set to $0.439$ following Reiter's 1992 PSI),
$E_{3 \rightarrow 2} = (1/4 - 1/9) \times 13.595$ eV.

