DEUTERIUM CHARGE EXCHANGE - KRSTIC DATA
dd_chargex.nc

    --Version 3.1--
These data were produced by ratecalc, revision 1.34, using dd_chargex.input,
revision 1.1, as the input file.  The fit in dd_chargex.input was based
on data obtained from P. S. Krstic of the CFADC. Their Web site,
http://www-cfadc.phy.ornl.gov, has the same data, but only down to
0.1 eV. Ratecalc was run in DEBUG mode for this purpose. The only
additional change is the manual insertion of the value of sigv_max,
3.8e-08, at the end of the file.

Note that the CFADC calculations assume that the particles
are indistinguishable (in a quantum mechanical sense). However, an
expression for the "spin exchange" cross section can be computed and
is given for these data. It becomes the classically defined charge exchange
cross section at energies above roughly 1 eV.

These cross section data are the third set to be used with the DEGAS 2
code. These are the most recent and are in agreement with the experimental
measurements by Newman et al. The fit provided by the Janev book (used
in some of the DEGAS 2 examples) predates the Newman data and should
be considered inaccurate at low energies, ~ 1 eV. The fit provided by
the Janev-Smith database (hchex.nc above) was based on a table of
values published by Barnett. Even though Barnett referenced the Newman
data, his values do not correspond to those from Newman at low energies.
Inexplicably, there are no other conflicting data referenced by Barnett
which could explain this discrepancy. Given the agreement between the 
Newman data, the CFADC calculations, and earlier calculations by 
Hunter and Kuriyan, we conclude that these CFADC data are the best
charge exchange cross sections. Further details and references for this
comparison will be added to the DEGAS 2 User's Manual.

