D REFLECTION ON MO, TRIM DATA SCALED FROM D ON FE
D_refl_strim_Mo.nc

     --Version 1.0--
The data for D reflection off Fe were extracted from EIRENE's TRIM file (now
in CVS). Using the reduced energy formalism, the equivalent data for D
on Mo were estimated. This file was generated by pmiwrite, as is. Unlike
the original EIRENE data, these have been interpolated onto uniform energy
and angle grids. Since EIRENE was mindlessly extrapolating the cumulative
distributions beyond the bounds of the data, we've extended the random
number mesh to include points at 0 and 1. In order to retain the original
data points (at 0.1, 0.3, etc.) and have a uniform mesh, the number of
data points expanded from 5 to 11. In comparisons with EIRENE, the lower
bound of the reflected energy proved particularly critical to the 
simulations. Hence, the minimum energy in the data file was selected so
as to mimic EIRENE's extrapolation procedure. Future runs of codes like
TRIM should make an attempt to estimate this lower energy bound.

     --Version 1.1--
Fill unused portion of main data table with real_unused. Also, mimic
EIRENE's extrapolation of cos(theta) at its lower bound (analogous to
procedure used for energy above). File is as generated by pmiwrite
v. 1.10.

